                "senderName": "NWS Pueblo CO",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 26 at 11:53AM MDT until October 28 at 5:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO",
                "description": "...The National Weather Service in Pueblo has issued a Flood Watch\nfor the following rivers in Colorado...\n\nPurgatoire River Near Las Animas affecting Las Animas Vicinity/Bent\nCounty zone.\n\nFor the Purgatoire River...including Las Animas...flooding is\npossible.\n\n* WHAT...High flow is traveling down the Upper Purgatoire from recent\nrains, and may lead to flooding near Las Animas.\n\n* WHERE...Purgatoire River near Las Animas.\n\n* WHEN...From this evening to Wednesday afternoon.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 11:15 AM MDT Monday the stage was 2.5 feet.\n- Forecast...Flood stage may be reached late this evening.\n- Flood stage is 9.0 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "If you are in the watch area, remain alert to possible flooding.\n\nPlease report observed flooding to local emergency services or law\nenforcement and request they pass this information to the National\nWeather Service when you can do so safely.\n\nStay tuned to further developments by listening to your local radio,\ntelevision, or NOAA Weather Radio for further information.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued this evening at 800 PM MDT.",
                "response": "Prepare",
