                "senderName": "NWS Honolulu HI",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 26 at 3:05AM HST until October 29 at 5:00AM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
                "description": "A trough moving over the state should bring abundant tropical\nmoisture and is expected to remain nearly stationary for a few days.\nHeavy rain and isolated thunderstorms are possible, potentially\nleading to flooding across all islands.\n\n* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...All main Hawaiian Islands.\n\n* WHEN...From Tuesday morning through late Wednesday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flood prone roads and other low lying areas may be closed\ndue to elevated runoff and overflowing streams. Urban areas may\nreceive more significant flooding and property damage due to rapid\nrunoff.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Heavy showers and isolated thunderstorms with intense rain rates\nmay develop Tuesday and continue through Wednesday evening as a\ntrough moves over the state.",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
                "response": "Prepare",
